commit d48feaced1c142566dad5cf93e9fb3d2e4486dc8
Author: Marius Momeu <marius.momeu@berkeley.edu>
Date:   Sat Nov 14 03:50:51 2026 +0000

    utf8.c: port/unexport 1 item (wave-232/batch-0/run-1)

    fn::git_utf8_char_length

    The export goes, with its raw binding and allowlist entry: no C the
    variants build calls it, its remaining callers being under GIT_WIN32
    alone. Its port, char_count, keeps its API. Its C test case,
    test_utf8__char_length (tests/util/utf8.c), carried over by
    char_count_carries_over_the_c_test, leaves c/ with the declaration in
    src/util/utf8.h: the fork's 9859ed5e7 (unexport git_utf8_char_length),
    which the submodule records. The variants' generation gen4 is built from
    it; the C tests over it give the baseline less that one case, and
    c-baseline.json moves by it. The dashboard's rows and Notes entry, the
    run's records, and the proposal later-stage-c-changes.

    Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>

